	(text "NOTES - rev 0.2\nIntended source: Mean Well RT-65B-type supply (+5V / +12V / -12V, 60 kHz).\nEach rail: PTC fuse, removable current link, then a pi filter (47uF - 10uH -\n1000uF with 10uF and 100nF ceramics). A Schottky diode from each rail to 0V\nstops a rail reversing and trips the fuse if a lead is swapped.\nLEDs sit after the fuses: a dark LED means no input or a tripped fuse.\nTP1-TP3 show what the supply delivers; J5-J8 show what the modules see.\nPull a JP link and put an ammeter across its pins to read rail current.\nChanges from rev 0.1a: 5V rail completed (bus, capacitors, terminal block),\nbead replaced by a 10uH inductor, bulk capacitance moved to the bus side,\nfour headers at 22 mm instead of six at 11.43 mm." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 142.24 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "73473b0a-00c1-5af8-b161-51d7a0cb4b44"))
